# Binds the hosted run locally: `npm run verify` runs against flatmate-io-dev before every push
# (F2 plan, section 7, decision 2; openspec/changes/ci-local-database, D7). The `verify-hosted`
# job in .github/workflows/ci.yml is the backstop for a push that skipped this with --no-verify —
# it runs the same suite against flatmate-io-dev on every push to main, just after the fact
# instead of before.
#
# Known costs, accepted by decision 2:
# - about 45s per push;
# - an Auth 429 ("Invalid credentials" from signIn) when a push follows a manual verify run
#   within about 5 minutes;
# - deleting a remote branch, and pushing a tag, also run the full suite;
# - this checks the working tree, not the commit being pushed — husky's normal behaviour, so
#   uncommitted edits count too.
npm run verify
